WEBVTT

00:09:29.064 --> 00:09:30.608
and then once we get there,

00:09:30.649 --> 00:09:33.902
we'll turn around and create
opportunities for others."

00:09:34.278 --> 00:09:35.654
The problem is,

00:09:35.696 --> 00:09:38.657
so many of us never seem to get there,

00:09:38.699 --> 00:09:39.908
and when we do,

00:09:39.950 --> 00:09:43.495
we become all-consumed
with maintaining our seat.

00:09:44.121 --> 00:09:46.290
One woman of color
we spoke to in the research

00:09:46.332 --> 00:09:48.334
gave us our greatest "drop the mic" moment

00:09:48.375 --> 00:09:49.501
when she said,

00:09:49.543 --> 00:09:53.464
"We're competing with other women
for a seat at the table.

00:09:53.505 --> 00:09:55.924
And there’s only one broke-ass chair.”

00:09:55.924 --> 00:09:57.259
And that's the problem.

00:09:57.760 --> 00:10:00.554
The designation of one seat